# width: 120
# height: 40
# The launcher dock's edge grip (src/ui/edge_grip.zig) under
# `ui.dock.placement = .outer`: `⋯` at the middle of the SCREEN's last
# row — the `:` line's row, cells 58..60 with the glyph on 59 at 120
# columns — and a strip that, revealed, PAINTS on that same row. That
# is what makes the `:` line's claim on it a contest, which is the
# whole subject of this file; `edge_grip_dock.test` is the default
# `.inner` placement, where the grip is on that row and the strip is
# not.
#
# The bar and the columns ship `.always`, so the only grip on this
# screen is the dock's.
write a.txt "alpha\n"
open a.txt
ex dock outer
expect screen contains "dock: below the command line"
# `auto_hide`, as mnml ships: nothing is drawn, and the grip says where.
expect screen lacks "New terminal"
expect screen contains "⋯"
# Dwelling on it reveals the strip, because the grip is INSIDE the
# dock's hover zone and not a second way in.
hover 59 39
wait 600
expect screen contains "New terminal"
# Away: the strip goes and the grip comes back.
hover 60 10
wait 800
expect screen lacks "New terminal"
expect screen contains "⋯"

# ── the revealed strip covers that row, the toast echo with it ──
# A toast's box fades after three seconds; its echo on the bottom row
# does not, which is the thing the strip is painting over.
ex dock labels
wait 3500
expect screen contains "dock: icons and labels"
hover 30 39
wait 600
expect screen contains "New terminal"
expect screen lacks "dock: icons and labels"
hover 60 10
wait 800

# ── an open `:` line takes the row back ──
# It refuses the reveal outright and the grip goes with it: typing is
# never covered.
key ctrl+;
expect status contains "\"cmdline\":true"
expect screen lacks "⋯"
hover 59 39
wait 600
expect screen lacks "New terminal"
expect status contains "\"cmdline\":true"
key esc
expect status contains "\"cmdline\":false"
hover 60 10

# ── a click on the grip pins, and never opens the `:` line ──
# The grip's hit is registered after the row's own and wins its cells.
click 59 39
expect screen contains "dock pinned"
expect status contains "\"cmdline\":false"
expect screen contains "New terminal"
expect screen lacks "⋯"

# ── pinned, the strip is the outermost row and the `:` line is above it ──
# A click on row 38 opens the line; one on the strip's own row 39 does
# not, which is the proof the two rows really swapped places.
click 110 38
expect status contains "\"cmdline\":true"
key esc
click 100 39
expect status contains "\"cmdline\":false"

# Unpinning hands the strip back to `ui.dock.mode`, and the grip with it.
command view.dock_pin
expect screen contains "dock: auto_hide"
hover 60 10
wait 800
expect screen lacks "New terminal"
expect screen contains "⋯"
